      "type": "picture",
      "imageAssetRef": "ag-asset://8497549f-2431-4a27-b201-836ffb2de8b7"
    },
    {
      "order": 12,
      "depth": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "content": "Surrounding the temple, there are 108 springs called Sahasradhara, which are perennial and have pure water throughout the year. The water is considered to be holy; thus, whenever a devotee visits this kshethram, they perform prokshanam of this water at each of the 108 springs.",
      "textFontSizeHint": 16
    }
  ]
